{
  "//": "Shared test vectors for logic that necessarily exists TWICE: once in Rust (apps/desktop/src/origin.rs, where the app answers \"what was this made from\") and once in TypeScript (packages/core/src/origin.ts, where the migrate-prompt script answers it with the app closed). Duplicated logic drifts — so both implementations are pinned by THESE cases, and a threshold change means editing this file and watching both suites fail.",
  "//phash": "A 16-character hex string, because a 64-bit hash does not survive a JSON number.",
  "//grey": "A flat colour signature: every one of the 192 bytes set to this value. Two rows therefore sit exactly |a - b| apart, which is what makes the colour cases readable.",
  "//thresholds": "hash > 3 (the dupe threshold) and <= 8; colour <= 16; strictly older; at most 12 hops. Measured on a 155,000-row library: 8 bits and colour 16 links 65% of img2img rows against 4% of txt2img ones, which have no source image and so are the negative control.",
